// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/idcode.t27 -- a JTAG IDCODE taken apart bit by bit, and named
; Source of truth for public/widgets/idcode/ (gHashTag/trinity): scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs
; compiles this file, checks its constants, evaluates the tests below and writes the page; the page
; hands every constant to tool.js as window.T27_WIDGET. tool.js holds no English of its own: every
; word on screen is a SAY_ constant here, every number the tool relies on is a K_ constant.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT DOES: the reader types or pastes a 32-bit IDCODE (or a whole openFPGALoader printout; the
; first hex word is taken). The page draws the 32 bits as buttons in the four IEEE 1149.1 fields --
; version [31:28], part number [27:12], manufacturer [11:1] and the fixed 1 in bit 0 -- splits the
; manufacturer into its JEP106 bank (continuation-code count plus one) and identity code, and then
; looks the code up the way openFPGALoader v1.1.1 does in src/jtag.cpp: the full IDCODE first, then
; with the version masked to 0. It shows the row it found (manufacturer, family, model, IR length),
; the lines `openFPGALoader --detect` would print for it, and a card the reader can save as a PNG.
; The URL hash keeps the code (#id=0x03636093), so a link reproduces the result.

; DATA PROVENANCE: parts.json is extracted by scripts/widget-data/idcode.mjs from openFPGALoader's
; src/part.hpp and src/board.hpp at tag v1.1.1 (commit 85be4fa02b2d), sha256-pinned; it is the
; whole fpga_list, misc_dev_list and list_manufacturer (about 16 KB), plus the part of nine boards.
; The bench numbers come from openFPGALoader 1.1.1 run on this project's own bench.

; WHAT THE BENCH SAID: on 2026-10-04 UTC one QMTech Wukong V1 was attached. With --verbose-level 2,
; openFPGALoader prints the raw word it shifted out: 0x13636093, version 1. Its --detect lines print
; idcode 0x3636093, because jtag.cpp stores the masked key it matched, not the raw word. So the
; 0x03636093 recorded for all three boards on 2026-08-17 (t27 fpga/HARDWARE_SSOT.md, W791) is the
; table key and the IDCODE our bitstreams carry; the raw word of the other two boards is not known
; to this page.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: a name for a manufacturer code outside openFPGALoader's nine-entry list
; (the page gives the bank and code to look up in JEDEC JEP106 instead), a device for a code outside
; its table, or anything about a device beyond its table row. The table has its own slips, shown as
; they are: one row's manufacturer bits do not say Xilinx (0x04ac4033), keys listed twice keep only
; the first row, and the zynqmp_cfgn rows end in a 0 bit, which IEEE 1149.1 does not allow.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

